Version 0.3.0
---------------------

  - Beta: please report problems on GitHub
  - FEATURE: Bento body (Max avatar) with fingers and a face that follow the Bento bones (Options > Bento body)
  - FEATURE: Show or hide joint groups: wings, tail, hind limbs, face, fingers and toes (Options > Joints)
  - FEATURE: The name of the joint under the mouse is shown next to the pointer
  - FEATURE: Male body shape (Figure: male)
  - FEATURE: Remote control for AI assistants and other programs (Options > Allow remote control, see docs/CONTROL.md); the MCP server is in the mcp folder
  - FEATURE: Linux build (AppImage)
  - Safer file reading: broken or hostile BVH, AVM, prop and mesh files are refused with a message instead of crashing
  - Data files are read from the program folder, never from the current folder
  - Saving reports errors and no longer leaves half-written files
  - Release downloads come with SHA256 checksums and signed build provenance


Version 0.2.0
---------------------

  - First PinglyMotion release, based on QAvimator
  - FEATURE: Bento skeleton with all 133 Second Life bones (fingers, face, tail, wings)
  - FEATURE: Dark theme and dockable panels
  - FEATURE: Update check now looks for new releases on GitHub
  - Builds with Qt 6


Version 0.1.1.450
---------------------

  - BUG: Fixed crash when loading props


Version 0.1.1
---------------------

  - BUG: Fixed avatar position interpolation
  - BUG: Fixed avatar rotation/position ignoring changes if return key was not pressed after typing a new value


Version 0.1.0
---------------------

  - First release
  - FEATURE: Added program update notifications
